NXR-231|Independent UART content oracle|Independent observer|The external checker shall validate expected per-worker content and sequence in addition to CRC and framing.|A valid CRC only proves consistency with the sender's bytes, not correct job execution.|A wrong payload with a recomputed valid CRC fails; a valid multiworker stream passes.|Feed synthetic UART waveforms and physical target streams with independent expected payload generation.|NXR-099|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Fixed per-worker oracle state and declared maximum worker count.|docs/hardware-in-loop.rst,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst|A valid CRC only proves consistency with the sender's bytes, not correct job execution.
NXR-232|Observer calibration identity|Independent observer|Every timing result shall identify checker clock, sampling resolution, synchronizer uncertainty and calibration validity.|An external clock is independent but still requires measurement uncertainty accounting.|Expired or mismatched calibration prevents a timing pass; known pulse widths fall within declared uncertainty.|Apply a reference pulse train at boundary widths and compare captured intervals.|NXR-099|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Calibration version and finite validity interval recorded per checker.|docs/hardware-in-loop.rst,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst|An external clock is independent but still requires measurement uncertainty accounting.
NXR-233|UART framing fault sensitivity|Independent observer|UART checker qualification shall detect wrong baud, stop-bit violations, truncated records and FIFO overrun distinctly.|Successful text decoding does not qualify framing and overload error detection.|Inject each fault independently and preserve the first affected byte or record identity.|Generate controlled waveforms and throttle the checker input sink.|NXR-099|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Declared baud tolerance, FIFO depth and maximum record length.|docs/hardware-in-loop.rst,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst|Successful text decoding does not qualify framing and overload error detection.
NXR-234|Physical latency witnesses|Independent observer|Latency tests shall measure stimulus arrival, handler entry and worker dispatch as separate physical events.|USB timestamps cannot separate interrupt latency from host transport latency.|A delayed worker with prompt ISR entry is classified as scheduling delay rather than interrupt-entry delay.|Drive an external stimulus and capture three GPIO witnesses with calibrated timestamps.|NXR-099|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Per-board limits declared before arming; GPIO overhead measured.|docs/hardware-in-loop.rst,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst|USB timestamps cannot separate interrupt latency from host transport latency.
NXR-235|Checker arming handshake|Independent observer|A target run requiring an observer shall start only after the matching checker run identity is armed and acknowledged.|An independently running checker can still observe the wrong target run without identity binding.|Unarmed, stale or wrong-profile checker rejects the run; target and checker terminal identities must match.|Race checker reset and host START while validating a physical start marker.|NXR-099|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|One active checker run and finite arming deadline.|docs/hardware-in-loop.rst,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst|An independently running checker can still observe the wrong target run without identity binding.
NXR-236|Checker fault injection controls|Independent observer|Each observer detection channel shall have a controlled injection proving it can fail the run.|An FPGA signature accumulator can appear healthy while its comparison or reporting path is disabled.|Disable a detector or alter a known-bad waveform; qualification detects the missing expected failure.|Run byte corruption, missing sequence, timing overrun and reset injections before acceptance tests.|NXR-099|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Finite preflight corpus and explicit injection-enabled profile.|docs/hardware-in-loop.rst,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst|An FPGA signature accumulator can appear healthy while its comparison or reporting path is disabled.
NXR-237|Reset observation provenance|Independent observer|The bench shall distinguish host-requested reset, watchdog reset, power interruption and unexplained reboot using available independent evidence.|A new boot counter alone cannot explain why the previous execution ended.|Controlled reset cases produce distinct evidence; unavailable reset-cause hardware yields unknown rather than a fabricated cause.|Correlate reset line, target boot identity and retained hardware reason where supported.|NXR-099|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Bounded reset event history and declared reset-domain wiring.|docs/hardware-in-loop.rst,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst|A new boot counter alone cannot explain why the previous execution ended.
NXR-238|Supply and disconnect domain|Independent observer|Power interruption tests shall document which target, bridge and checker domains lose power and preserve evidence outside the tested domain.|USB power wiring can reset the evidence collector along with the target.|Target-only power cycling does not erase checker evidence; shared-power loss is explicitly classified incomplete.|Execute the declared wiring matrix and verify reconnect identity and retained files.|NXR-099|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Equipment current and voltage limits declared per board; no undeclared reset assumptions.|docs/hardware-in-loop.rst,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst|USB power wiring can reset the evidence collector along with the target.
NXR-239|RISCue hardware claim boundary|Independent observer|RISCue RTL, ECC and TMR hardware claims shall require the corresponding FPGA image and observable counters rather than commercial RISC-V silicon alone.|A compatible ISA does not implement the custom processor's redundancy or protection hardware.|A commercial MCU run is accepted only for its HAL scope; absent ECC or TMR support cannot receive a hardware pass.|Validate image hashes, feature manifests and one controlled hardware event per claimed detector.|NXR-099|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Declared FPGA image and exposed counter widths; unsupported checks skipped explicitly.|docs/hardware-in-loop.rst,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst|A compatible ISA does not implement the custom processor's redundancy or protection hardware.
NXR-240|Observer storage overflow result|Independent observer|A checker shall report capture loss and withhold complete-trace or timing-pass claims after overflow.|An apparently valid tail of captured output can hide dropped earlier failures.|Exceed FIFO and capture depth; loss counters and terminal incomplete status appear while a bounded control passes.|Drive maximal-rate streams and delayed host drains at the declared input limit.|NXR-099|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Fixed FIFO and capture RAM; no silent circular overwrite of mandatory first-fault evidence.|docs/hardware-in-loop.rst,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst|An apparently valid tail of captured output can hide dropped earlier failures.
